---
title: Khao piek sen
tags: [lao, chicken, pork, weekend]
cuisine: lao
source: Khao Piek Sen by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/khao-piek-sen
---

== Broth ==

Bring a #large stockpot{} of @water{} to a boil over high heat. Add the
@chicken{1}(whole stewing hen), @carrot{1}, @ginger{1%knob},
@garlic{4%cloves}, @cilantro roots{3}, @palm sugar{2%pieces},
@soy sauce{3%tbsp}, @chicken bouillon{2%tbsp} and @kosher salt{2%tbsp}.

Lower the heat and simmer until the broth turns golden brown. Strain and
discard the vegetables. Shred the hen's meat and keep it aside.

Season the broth with more @soy sauce{} and salt. Refrigerate the broth and
meat separately.

== Rice noodles ==

Put the @tapioca starch{1%bag}, @rice flour{1 1/2%bags}(jasmine) and
@glutinous rice flour{2%tbsp} in a bowl and pour in @water{4%cup}(boiling).
Mix with an #immersion blender{} until even.

Knead on a floured surface into a smooth ball. Cover with a damp towel and rest
~{20%minutes}.

Roll out and cut into noodles of the thickness you like. Dust with more
@rice flour{} and keep covered with a damp towel.

== Pork meatballs ==

Blend the @ground pork{500%g}, @cornstarch{15%g}, @kosher salt{5%g},
@fish sauce{1%tbsp}, @neutral oil{1%tbsp}, @baking powder{1%tsp},
@granulated sugar{1%tsp}, @ground black pepper{1/2%tsp} and
@water{75%ml}(cold) in a #food processor{}. Chill ~{1%hour}.

Roll into even balls and drop them into boiling water. When they float, lift
them out.

== To serve ==

Heat some broth in a #saucepan{} over medium heat with some of the shredded
hen, meatballs and noodles. Cook ~{3%minutes}, until heated through and the
noodles turn translucent.

Pour into a bowl and finish with @cilantro{}, @scallions{}, @lime juice{},
@chile oil{}, @crispy garlic{}, @fried shallots{} and @pa thong ko{}.

> Pa thong ko is fried dough, like a Chinese cruller.
